{
  "name": "Linguistics - BA - Language Studies",
  "kind": "major",
  "type": "Bachelor's Degree",
  "department": "Linguistics",
  "source": "https://catalog.ucsd.edu/curric/LING-ug.html",
  "narrative": [
    "Students majoring in language studies must consult with the language studies faculty adviser to approve an individual curricular plan.",
    "Each language studies major will specialize in one language of concentration.",
    "Note: at least two of the upper-division courses must be conducted in the language of concentration.",
    "For the language studies major, at least six out of the twelve upper division courses counted toward the major must be taken at UC San Diego, and at least four of these must be linguistics courses that satisfy Part A of the language studies course requirements.",
    "Students whose language of concentration is American Sign Language will need to consult the faculty adviser for individualized requirements.",
    "Except for LIGN 188R, LIGN 195, LIGN 199, and LIGN 199H, no course taken on a Pass/Not Pass basis may be counted toward a linguistics major. No more than four combined units of LIGN 188R, LIGN 195, and LIGN 199 may be counted toward a linguistics major. An additional four units of LIGN 199H may be counted toward a linguistics major.",
    "A letter grade of C– or better is required for every course counted toward a linguistics major, including courses taken to satisfy the department’s undergraduate language requirement.",
    "LIGN 87 and LIGN 192 do not count as linguistics electives (restricted courses).",
    "The page calls this the \"Language Studies Major\" (twelve upper-division courses: six linguistics, two literature, four additional); the general undergraduate language requirement for other linguistics majors does not apply to it."
  ],
